{"availability":"available","full":"plimsollmark/plimsoll","name":"plimsoll","description":"A sandbox service for running untrusted, agent-authored code that reports the isolation boundary each run executed behind. Lessons, no clone needed: https://plimsollmark.github.io/plimsoll/trainers/","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":9,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-10T20:07:00Z","updated":"2026-10-12T01:39:29Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://plimsollmark.github.io/plimsoll/","topics":["ai-agents","code-execution","code-interpreter","e2b","firecracker","golang","gvisor","llm-agents","mcp","sandbox","security","self-hosted","webassembly"],"demo":"https://plimsollmark.github.io/plimsoll/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z","stars":9,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["plimsoll runs untrusted code, such as code an AI agent wrote, inside a sandbox, and every result says how strong that sandbox was. A request can demand a minimum strength; if the sandbox is weaker, nothing runs.","The name comes from the Plimsoll line, the load limit painted on the outside of a ship's hull where anyone can check it. plimsoll does the same for the isolation tier: how strong the wall around a run is, stated as one of four levels, weakest first: process, container, kernel, vm. The tier is a value on every result, not a sentence in a datasheet. A request can set a floor, the weakest tier it will accept, and the official Go client checks the tier again when the result comes back.","The same machinery lets plimsoll run an exam on code an agent wrote, not only contain it. A trial runner built into the simulation image runs the agent's program against scenarios that program cannot read: each one reaches the runner in a file deleted before the program starts. Every run returns SHA-256 hashes of the request as sent and the result as returned, which the official clients recompute (how). A separate program outside the daemon, plimsoll-attest, signs the checked results, refuses a chain of calls with one missing, and replays a run. The exam itself (the simulated system, the…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/plimsollmark/plimsoll/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c658040ef780a1fd8382b883813d0c087dca6782524718fb4f4a95f3e7850bb6","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"plimsoll runs untrusted code, such as code an AI agent wrote, inside a sandbox, and every result says how strong that sandbox was. A request can demand a minimum strength; if the sandbox is weaker, nothing runs.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/plimsollmark/plimsoll/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"How this compares with the other self-hosted sandboxes for agent code (E2B's self-hosted version, microsandbox, NVIDIA OpenShell, Kubernetes agent-sandbox and eight more), each described from its own documentation, with plimsoll's weak points beside them: the comparison (INTERNAL · plimsoll site →).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/plimsollmark/plimsoll/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"c658040ef780a1fd8382b883813d0c087dca6782524718fb4f4a95f3e7850bb6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/plimsollmark/plimsoll/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-12T01:39:29Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/plimsollmark/plimsoll/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T02:00:42.647Z","hash":"c658040ef780a1fd8382b883813d0c087dca6782524718fb4f4a95f3e7850bb6","originalBytes":27658,"storedBytes":27658,"truncated":false,